WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.120
Skywalker has risen and the nine-part Skywalker
saga has ended.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.660
We've misplaced our Jedi Holocrons nd our
Sith Wayfinder accidentally got flushed down

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.750
the space-toilet, so all we can do is make
some educated guesses about what the ending

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.740
of Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker all meant.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.600
Spoilers incoming.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:24.260
For a movie franchise that's generally regarded
as science fiction, there sure are a lot of

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:29.240
supernatural and probably ectoplasmic beings
hanging around the galaxy in Star Wars.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.280
Of course, we're used to seeing Force Ghosts
by now.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:37.240
Ever since Obi Wan told Luke to turn off his
dang iPhone so he could shoot his torpedoes

00:00:37.249 --> 00:00:41.449
into the Death Star's exhaust port, fans have
accepted the fact that when you're strong

00:00:41.449 --> 00:00:44.980
with the Force, you get to play extra innings
as a glowing blue person.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:50.100
And when Yoda himself showed up in The Last
Jedi to mess with Luke and set an old tree

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:55.219
on fire, it became clear that the Force Ghosts
in Star Wars were going to do a bit more than

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:57.120
dispense wisdom and exposition.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:05.650
So that's our best guess as to who - or what
- that crowd of creeps might've been hanging

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:10.600
around with Emperor Palpatine on Exegol at
the movie's end: Force Ghosts.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:15.210
Palpatine made a big deal about how all of
the Sith were fueling him, and it seemed as

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:19.140
though the hooded figures who faded in and
out of view during the scenes with the Emperor

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.780
were some kinds of spectral Sith lords.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:26.970
Meanwhile, Rey's cosmic pep talk at the end
of the film came courtesy of Jedi Force Ghosts

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.720
— and even featured the voice talents of
Jedi actors past and present, including Hayden

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:37.370
Christensen and Ewan MacGregor reprising their
roles as Anakin Skywalker and Obi-Wan Kenobi

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:39.700
from the prequel trilogy, among many others.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.720
One of the most dramatic plot developments
in the film came in the form of Kylo Ren's

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:49.420
reversal and transformation back into his
previous identity of Ben Solo.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.300
His redemption was one that was preordained
from the first moment we learned he was Han

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.460
and Leia's son in The Force Awakens.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:01.970
Not only that, but he's this trilogy's version
of Darth Vader, who himself had a rather famous

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.500
redemption of his own at the end of Return
of the Jedi.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:09.400
As such, the chance that he would close out
the series as a full villain seemed pretty

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:09.900
remote.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:15.480
Even still, Kylo Ren's turnaround might've
seemed kind of abrupt, so why and how did

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.580
he turn to the light?

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.940
Even though he ended each film playing the
part of the villain, Kylo Ren expressed conflict

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:26.590
and doubts about his ability to fully commit
to the First Order and the Dark Side in each

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:27.080
episode.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:33.040
With each film, Ren seemed unable to fully
accept his decision to go bad - and in so

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:37.910
doing, acted out like an angry baby, slashing
consoles with his lightsaber, and smashing

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.200
his helmet out of frustration.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:45.140
So when Leia expended all her willpower trying
to reach her son one last time - apparently

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:50.540
going so far as to pull an Obi Wan to sacrifice
herself for the good of her kid - it may have

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:53.540
opened the door for him to actually see the
light side again.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:59.680
From there, Rey's own sacrifice of her Force
energy to heal the fatal wound she dealt him

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.060
probably sealed the deal.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:07.000
Near the very end of the film, Maz Kanata
hands Chewbacca a cute little medal, saying

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.920
that Leia would've wanted him to have it.

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:13.260
The moment kind of comes out of nowhere, but
chances are good that folks in theaters were

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.040
pretty happy when the scene unfolded.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:19.860
If you're wondering why, the answer can be
found 42 years in the past.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:25.660
Back at the end of the first Star Wars film,
A New Hope, Han and Luke are awarded medals

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:30.140
by Princess Leia in a ceremony that's full
of smiles and great John Williams music.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:34.620
But despite having just as much to do with
her rescue and the destruction of the Death

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.120
Star as anyone, poor Chewbacca didn't get
jack squat.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:43.360
Chewie's medal neglect has been a sore point
for Star Wars fans for decades, so it's only

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.280
fitting that he finally gets his due in this
last movie.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:51.500
Additionally, the medal was probably the one
Leia had originally given to Chewbacca's life-mate

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.319
Han, which gives the moment even more significance.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.010
So what was this movie actually about?

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:03.580
Well, beyond the obvious answer of "wars...in
the stars," this is a movie that pins its

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:06.200
emotional core on the idea of togetherness.

00:04:06.489 --> 00:04:11.280
To lay it out simply, The Rise of Skywalker
is about how working together is good, and

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:12.660
going it alone is bad.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:17.880
It sounds pretty corny when it's put that
way, but the strength of that theme is undeniable.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:23.800
Think about it: Rey can't succeed without
help from Ben Solo, and in the end she relies

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:27.480
on the will of all the past Jedi to help her
defeat Palpatine.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:32.020
Moreover, Finn and Poe go to great lengths
to keep their party together this time around.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:36.960
This is all in stark contrast to the events
of The Last Jedi, a movie that also proves

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:41.160
the same theme to be true, though it does
so in the exact opposite way.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:47.430
When Finn and Rose break off from the Resistance
to help Poe undermine Admiral Holdo, disaster

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:47.920
follows.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:52.760
And Luke's decision to abandon his sister
and the Republic leaves the galaxy open to

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:57.990
the rise of the First Order - as well as,
apparently, the rise of the Final Order and

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.500
the resurrection of the Emperor.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:05.000
Meanwhile, Rey and Kylo Ren's connection in
The Last Jedi set up their deeper alliance

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:09.600
in The Rise of Skywalker, and eventually led
to the final destruction of the Empire.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:15.960
That connection is fully realized at the end,
when she takes on his family's name of Skywalker

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:19.500
and completely embraces her adopted family
as her actual one.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:25.820
So with the end of the First Order, the Final
Order, the Emperor, and the Supreme Leader,

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:27.320
who's in charge of the galaxy now?

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:32.100
If your answer is the Republic, well, you're
wrong there too, since they got exploded back

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:32.820
in The Force Awakens.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:38.340
It's an easy detail to forget, since we never
really got to see what Leia's newly established

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:43.400
New Republic could do as an intergalactic
governing body, but maybe it's just as well.

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:47.860
The answer to the question of who's in charge
is, basically, no one.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:52.900
The free planets are free, and maybe a new
galactic government will get together to debate

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:55.720
trade routes and taxation, just like the good
ol' days.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.220
Or maybe they won't!

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:01.520
Or maybe Rey will decide to take on the role
of Empress after all - but she'll be a good

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:06.080
one, and she'll rename the Star Destroyers
something nicer… like Star Deployers.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:07.900
There's no end to the possibilities!

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:13.490
The final scene of the film shows Rey burying
the two lightsabers that once belonged to

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:16.680
Luke and Leia at the Lars family homestead
on Tatooine.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:21.060
It's a nice scene that symbolically plants
seeds for the future of this franchise in

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:22.160
an interesting way.

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:27.420
Even though the Skywalker Saga has come to
an end, the galaxy is still an awfully big

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:31.940
place full of people who'll find connections
to the Force, and may end up searching for

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:32.440
answers.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:38.160
That may lead them to Tatooine, which could
potentially become a holy site to future generations

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.180
of Force users.

00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:44.100
The future of Star Wars as a film franchise
is a huge question mark, though we know that

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:49.461
Kevin Feige, the architect of the mega-successful
Marvel Cinematic Universe, is working on his

00:06:49.461 --> 00:06:51.860
own ideas for forthcoming Star Wars movies.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:58.400
Whether we ever see Finn, Poe, Rey, or even
Lando or Chewbacca ever again remains to be

00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:58.900
seen.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:02.740
But while those lightsabers may be buried
in the sand, it stands to reason that we'll

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:08.040
see those legendary weapons from a galaxy
far, far away again before too long…

